  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0166 database is a retail store management system that stores information about products, customers, employees, and transactions. It has 16 tables, each with a specific purpose and structure.\nThe BRAND table contains information about the brands of products, including their ID, name, and email address. The COLOR table contains information about the colors of products, including their code and name. The CATEGORY table contains information about the categories of products, including their ID and name. The SIZE table contains information about the sizes of products, including their code and description. The GENDER table contains information about the genders of products, including their ID and name.\nThe TYPE table contains information about the types of products, including their ID, name, and category. The PRODUCT table contains information about the products themselves, including their ID, type, size, color, name, brand, gender, description, and price. The EMPLOYEE table contains information about the employees who work at the store, including their ID, first name, last name, date of birth, email, and phone number. The CUSTOMER table contains information about the customers who shop at the store, including their ID, first name, last name, date of birth, email, and phone number.\nThe CCPAYMENT_STATE table contains information about the payment states of credit card transactions, including their code and description. The CCPAYMENT table contains information about the credit card transactions themselves, including their ID, payment type, expected amount, approved amount, payment state, and time created, updated, and expired. The CCPAYMENT_TYPE table contains information about the types of credit card payments, including their code and description. The CCENTRY_METHOD table contains information about the methods of credit card entry, including their code and description.\nThe CCPAYMENT_CARD table contains information about the credit cards used for payment, including their ID, payment type, is encryption, card number, bank name, expiration date, and entry method. The TICKET table contains information about the sales tickets, including their ID, time placed, employee ID, customer ID, total product, total tax, total order, and credit card payment ID. The TICKET_ITEM table contains information about the items on the sales tickets, including their ticket ID, sequence number, product ID, quantity, price, tax amount, and product amount.\nOverall, the schemabench_0166 database is a comprehensive system for managing a retail store, including information about products, customers, employees, and transactions. It uses a variety of tables and relationships to store and retrieve this information, making it easy to manage and analyze the data.",
  "gold_question": "Small Fashion Shop \n\n 1) Background / Context\nA local fashion retailer is struggling with managing their inventory and gaining insights into customer preferences due to a lack of digital storage systems for inventory, sales, and payment data. This inefficiency impacts their ability to maintain competitiveness in the market.\n\n 2) Objectives\nThe primary objective is to develop a structured database system to store product, sales, and payment information. The system should allow for generation of business insights and recommendations by querying the database.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n- Stakeholders: \n  - Shop Owners: Interested in high-level business insights and sales performance.\n  - Managers: Need detailed inventory management and sales reporting.\n  \n- Users: \n  - Employees: Will interact with the system for transaction processing and inventory updates.\n  - Customers: Indirect users whose purchase data informs business insights.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n- Database Design and Implementation:\n  - Create tables for storing brand, product, sales, payment, and customer data.\n  - Maintain relationships between entities (e.g., products and categories).\n  \n- Inventory Management:\n  - Track product details such as color, size, and brand.\n  - Update inventory based on sales transactions.\n  \n- Sales and Payment Processing:\n  - Record sales tickets, including employee and customer information, product details, and pricing.\n  - Handle credit card payment information, ensuring state and type are recorded.\n  \n- Business Insights and Reporting:\n  - Analyze data to identify top-selling products and customer preferences.\n  - Generate reports for sales performance and inventory status.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Performance: \n  - Efficient querying to quickly retrieve business insights.\n  - Capable of handling concurrent transactions without degradation.\n  \n- Security:\n  - Protect sensitive customer and payment information.\n  - Ensure compliance with data protection regulations.\n  \n- Scalability: \n  - Allow for future expansion to accommodate more products and customers.\n  \n- Usability:\n  - Provide user-friendly interfaces for employees to update and access information.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0166.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0166\nCREATE TABLE `brand` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `color` (\n  `code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `category` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `size` (\n  `code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `gender` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `type` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `category_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `type_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`category_id`) REFERENCES `category` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `product` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `type_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `size_code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `color_code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `brand_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `gender_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `product_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`type_id`) REFERENCES `type` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `product_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`size_code`) REFERENCES `size` (`code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `product_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`color_code`) REFERENCES `color` (`code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `product_ibfk_4` FOREIGN KEY (`brand_id`) REFERENCES `brand` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `product_ibfk_5` FOREIGN KEY (`gender_id`) REFERENCES `gender` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `date_of_birth` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `date_of_birth` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ccpayment_state` (\n  `code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ccpayment` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `payment_type` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `expected_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `approved_amount` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `payment_state` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `time_created` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `time_updated` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `time_expired` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `ccpayment_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`payment_state`) REFERENCES `ccpayment_state` (`code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ccpayment_type` (\n  `code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ccentry_method` (\n  `code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ccpayment_card` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `payment_type` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `is_encryption` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  `card_number` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `bank_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `expiration_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `entry_method` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `ccpayment_card_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`payment_type`) REFERENCES `ccpayment_type` (`code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `ccpayment_card_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`entry_method`) REFERENCES `ccentry_method` (`code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ticket` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `time_placed` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `total_product` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `total_tax` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `total_order` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `credit_card_payment_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `ticket_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `ticket_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `ticket_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`credit_card_payment_id`) REFERENCES `ccpayment` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ticket_item` (\n  `ticket_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sequence_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `tax_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `product_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`ticket_id`, `sequence_number`),\n  CONSTRAINT `ticket_item_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`ticket_id`) REFERENCES `ticket` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `ticket_item_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
